GLibTest - riscos-gtk M1 test

Checks the GLib 2.80 build that riscos-gtk (GTK 3 for RISC OS) sits on:
the main loop (timeouts, idle, a nested loop), threads (GCond, a
GThreadPool with results sent back to the main loop), GIO (reading and
writing files, an asynchronous read on a worker thread, directory
listing), GObject signals, GVariant, GRegex, iconv, UTF-8, key files,
dates and printf.

Double-click !GLibTest. A task window shows lines "ok N - ..." and ends
with "glibtest: N checks, F failed". The same output is saved in the
Result file inside the application: send that file back, with a note of
anything else that happened (an error box, other tasks misbehaving).

Needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan).
PThreadTicker 0.03 is included (from riscos-unixlib 5.0.3.1).

riscos-gtk is MIT licensed; GLib, PCRE2, libffi and zlib keep their own
licences (GLib: LGPL-2.1-or-later). Built with riscos-crossdev 1.2.
